                "text": "**Analyzing Grid Patterns**\n\nOkay, I'm now focused on representing each row as either a 0 or a 1, where 1 signifies a row of 3s. My example clarifies the concept: a grid of varying heights with rows of 0s and rows of 3s. I'm exploring how to abstract this to build the representation in a more formal manner.\n\n\n**Observing Reversal Patterns**\n\nI've been analyzing the segments of '3' rows and how their order changes. The key insight is that the lengths of these segments are reversed in the output. I need to determine if this reversal is consistent across all cases and if there are other patterns related to the zeros that might be in the input to the process. Example 2 seems to be more complex.\n\n\n",
